-- A type error in an operand names the operator as it is written.

GIVEN `the applicant is a resident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may apply` IF
         `the applicant is a resident`
  UNLESS 18

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a number before UNLESS` IF 18 UNLESS FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception that is itself negated` IF TRUE UNLESS NOT 4

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a number after NOT` IF NOT 3

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a conjunction in parentheses` IS (TRUE AND 5)

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a conjunction written as a symbol` IS TRUE && 5

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a sum written as a symbol` IS 1 + TRUE

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a sum written as a word` IS TRUE PLUS 1

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `a list with a number for its tail` IS 1 FOLLOWED BY 2
